# Release

When the user asks to push, tag, or release a version, follow [docs/RELEASES.md](docs/RELEASES.md).

Before any `git push` of `main` or a `v*` tag:

1. Bump `Cargo.toml`, the top `CHANGELOG.md` heading, and the first metainfo `<release>` together. Never reuse a tag, even if the GitHub Release failed.
2. On Linux (`wijitify-vm` from Windows), run `python3 scripts/release-precheck.py vX.Y.Z`.
3. Push only after that script exits 0. It runs fmt, clippy, tests, and the Flatpak `cargo --offline build --release --locked` line with vendor patches applied.

Do not push a tag to see if Actions will compile it.
